@page "/"
@layout NFHotel.Web.Components.Layout.PublicLayout

@*
    The front page. Pure markup without a ViewModel, because the page fetches no data — it must be able to
    be shown even when the database is down, so the way to /book never closes.

    All content comes from nfhotel.com. Nothing is deliberately made up here:
    no phone number, no street number, no check-in times, no number of rooms.
    If it is not on the hotel's own page, it is not here.
*@

<PageTitle>NFHotel &amp; Bar — Street 172, Phnom Penh</PageTitle>

<section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-body">
        <span class="eyebrow">Street 172 &middot; Phnom Penh, Cambodia</span>

        <h1 class="display">NFHotel &amp; Bar</h1>

        <p class="lede">
            Comfortable, quiet rooms in the middle of everything. At NFHotel there is
            barely a reason to head out: the kitchen, the bar and reception are open
            around the clock, and we have nightly, monthly and short-term rates.
        </p>

        <div class="row">
            <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/book">Book your stay</a>
            <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="#rooms">See our rooms</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<div class="page stack-lg">

    <div class="grid-auto">
        <div class="stat">
            <div class="stat-value">24h</div>
            <div class="stat-label">Bar &amp; kitchen</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
            <div class="stat-value">172</div>
            <div class="stat-label">The street we're on</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
            <div class="stat-value">$20</div>
            <div class="stat-label">Per night, from</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
            <div class="stat-value">2023</div>
            <div class="stat-label">Renovated in November</div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid-3">
        <section class="card card-pad stack" id="rooms">
            <h2 class="subtitle">Rooms</h2>
            <p>
                Comfortable, quiet rooms from $20 a night. Fully renovated in
                November 2023.
            </p>
            <p class="muted">
                Nightly, monthly and short-term rates — tailored to whatever budget
                you're travelling on.
            </p>
            <a class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm" href="/book">See available rooms</a>
        </section>

        <section class="card card-pad stack">
            <h2 class="subtitle">Food &amp; bar</h2>
            <p>
                Burgers, local specialities and ice-cold draught beer. The kitchen and
                the bar are open 24 hours a day.
            </p>
            <p class="muted">
                You never have to leave the building for dinner — or for breakfast at
                four in the morning.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="card card-pad stack">
            <h2 class="subtitle">Finding us</h2>
            <p>
                We're on Street 172 in Phnom Penh, Cambodia — one of the liveliest
                streets in the city.
            </p>
            <p class="muted">
                Questions before you book? Write to
                <a href="mailto:help@nfhotel.com">help@nfhotel.com</a>.
                Reception is staffed around the clock.
            </p>
        </section>
    </div>

    <div class="row-between">
        <p class="lede">Ready to pick your dates?</p>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/book">Book your stay</a>
    </div>
</div>
